  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failure diagnosed \u2014 **inode exhaustion on upload filesystem, not app / DB / permissions**.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n- App container `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` `Up 21 seconds` (E1) (E5), with `restart_count 0`, `oom_killed false` (E5), bind `source /srv/lab-data -> destination /data rw:true` and user `1000:1000` (E5).\n- DB container `incidentlab-db-1` is `running` `Up 26 seconds (healthy)` (E1), `health healthy` (E10), logs `database system is ready to accept connections` with no error (E8).\n- App `/health` returns `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2).\n- App logs show `POST /upload 500` with `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device: '/data/tmp/*.part'` (E4) and health-check `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device: '/data/uploads/.health-*'` with `GET /health 503` (E4).\n- That `/data` path is the bind-mount from `/srv/lab-data` (E5), whose filesystem shows `use_percent 37.3` with `available_mb 282.9` but `inode_use_percent 100.0` (E6).\n- Root `/` filesystem is healthy `use_percent 6.8 inode_use_percent 1.5` (E9), isolating the problem to `/srv/lab-data` mountpoint (E6) vs (E9).\n- Permissions ruled out: `/srv/lab-data/uploads` `owner 1000:1000 mode 0755 app_user_can_write true` (E7) and `/srv/lab-data` `owner 1000:1000 mode 0755 app_user_can_write true` (E11) matching `user 1000:1000` (E5).\n- Recreate event at `23:47:14` for both containers then `start` (E3) is not the cause; both stay `running` after (E1)(E5)(E10).\n\n**Root cause vs symptoms:**\nRoot cause is 100% inode consumption on `/srv/lab-data` (E6) preventing any new file creation on `/data/tmp` and `/data/uploads` (E4)(E5). `500` on upload and `503` on health (E2)(E4) are symptoms of that `Errno 28` (E4).\n\nNeeds inode cleanup (many small files) on `/srv/lab-data` filesystem \u2014 block space is still available (E6).\n",
